=============================================================================
Upstream Submodules, Datasets, and Attributions
=============================================================================

1. HackerTube Dataset (https://hackertube.org/data)
   Created by Andrej Karpathy, derived from open-index/hacker-news
   (https://huggingface.co/datasets/open-index/hacker-news).
   Licensed under Open Data Commons Attribution License (ODC-By 1.0):
   https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/by/1-0/
   Modified: Extracted canonical YouTube video IDs and channel names into
   extension/assets/seeds/hn-videos.txt and hn-channels.txt.

2. AiSList (vendor/AiSList - https://github.com/Override92/AiSList)
   Created by Override92 and contributors.
   Licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International
   (CC BY-NC 4.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/
   Non-commercial use only. Provided as-is without warranties.
   Modified: Normalized channel handles and IDs into
   extension/assets/seeds/slop-channels.txt.

3. DeArrow Community Database (https://github.com/ajayyy/DeArrow)
   Created by Ajay Ramachandran and DeArrow contributors.
   Data licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
   (CC BY-SA 4.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
   Queried via k-anonymous 4-character SHA-256 hash prefixes against the public
   read-only mirror (https://dearrow.minibomba.pro/sbserver/).
   Community-picked thumbnail frames are loaded from https://dearrow-thumb.ajay.app.

4. Control Panel for Twitter (https://github.com/insin/control-panel-for-twitter), credited by the
   original Sieve
   Copyright (c) Jonathan Buchanan (insin). Licensed under the MIT License.

5. Slop Filter for X (https://github.com/midego1/slop-filter-for-x), credited by the
   original Sieve
   Licensed under the MIT License.

6. FocusTube (https://github.com/malekwael229/FocusTube), credited by
   the original Sieve
   Copyright (c) Malek Wael. Licensed under the MIT License.

7. xrai / rai (https://github.com/phuaky/xrai), credited by the original Sieve
   Licensed under the MIT License.

8. JetBrains Mono (https://www.jetbrains.com/lp/mono/)
   Copyright (c) JetBrains s.r.o. Licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.

9. Anthropic TypeScript SDK (https://github.com/anthropics/anthropic-sdk-typescript)
   Copyright (c) Anthropic, PBC. Licensed under the Apache License 2.0.
   Bundled into extension/dist/background.js for the Claude grader option.
   Full license text: licenses/anthropic-sdk-typescript-APACHE-2.0.txt

10. Kagi Small Web (https://github.com/kagisearch/smallweb)
    Copyright (c) Kagi Inc. Licensed under the MIT License.
    Used: YouTube channel IDs from smallyt.txt, merged into
    extension/assets/seeds/hn-channels.txt (keep list).

11. Wikidata (https://www.wikidata.org)
    Structured data released under CC0 1.0 (public domain dedication).
    Used: YouTube channel IDs (P2397) of photographers, filmmakers, animators,
    film directors, painters, sculptors, graphic designers and architects,
    merged into extension/assets/seeds/hn-channels.txt (keep list).

12. AiSList warnlist (same source and license as item 2, CC BY-NC 4.0)
    Used: extension/assets/seeds/slop-warn-channels.txt.

13. Return YouTube Dislike (https://returnyoutubedislike.com)
    Public API used at runtime for dislike counts, credited per its usage
    rights (attribution; at most 100 requests a minute, 10,000 a day).
